PATCH 391: AZER2 twin #2 -- reconstruct FUN_0000_3823 (per-object sprite render) base-losses; fix the
mission crash at 3823+0x74 (SIGSEGV fault-addr 0xffff), the next twin after patch 390's c7ca fix.

Runtime (setarch -R, FIST_SEGV_BT/EBP, clean patch-390 binary): EIP 0x0805c1ff = FUN_0000_3823+0x74,
fault-addr 0xffff; EBP chain 00d0->cae6->e714->459a->22dd->378e->3823.  3823 is a per-object SPRITE render
dispatched from 378e's object walk (obj in BX at entry -> C param_3=obj DGROUP near offset; param_2=cx).

asm 0x3823-0x38a9 base-losses reconstructed (all vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin):
 (1) sprite-directory resolution: es=word[DGROUP:0x4f0]; les es:(word[obj+0x32]); hdr=word[sprite-4].
     Ghidra dropped ES + the les indirection -> `*(undefined4*)*(undefined2*)(param_3+0x32)` deref'd the
     sprite id (0xffff sentinel on AZER2's type-1 objects) as a raw host ptr = the 0xffff fault.
 (2) FB-plot segment: es=word[dg+word[0x156a]] = word[vp+0]; Ghidra wrote the plot to a raw offset.
 (3) rowtable read: word[dg + X*2 + word[DGROUP:0x794]] (cf. the working pattern at build/fist.c:12442).
 (4) DAT_1000_d56a is (int*) = 4-byte stride under gcc -m32, but the asm reads word[di+0xa]/[+0xc]/[0];
     cast to uint16_t* so [5]/[6]/[0] mean +0xa/+0xc/+0 (Ghidra's int=2 hid this; gcc int=4 = +20/+24 = wrong).
 (5) Ghidra's `2c1c = 2c18 + (uVar4 & 0xff)` is a WIDTH error -- asm `add dx,ax` adds the full 16-bit hdr word.
All obj derefs (param_3+0x32, param_3+5) rebased to dg+obj; c6c8 blit (DGROUP:0x6c8) + c403f(obj) tail
unchanged.  Reached only on the in-mission object-render walk; the menu/settings/editor flows never enter it.

VALIDATED: AZER1 + CYPRUS1 mission-cockpit central-chrome AE=0 (43-flow verify both = 43/43, no regression);
AZER2 advances past 3823.  re_out/fist.c pristine 61453e42; make check clean.

